</table>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>A comparison between methods regarding shift-aware ability, computational efficiency (time &amp; space), and ability to handle infinite-state &amp; Deep-RL.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">That said, QUCB and the methods mentioned above only consider the finite-horizon episodic MDP setting, where reward and transition functions can change within an episode but are fixed across different episodes. Similarly, in the infinite-horizon discounted MDP, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. (2020)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al. (2021)</a></cite> assume the transition function is fixed across time steps. This is a strong assumption because the transition function can suddenly change in the real world. Therefore, we study a more challenging and realistic scenario by considering non-stationary RL under distribution shifts, i.e., the transition function can additionally change at a particular episode in the finite-horizon episodic MDP, or at a time step in the infinite-horizon discounted MDP. These settings are critical and align with real-world applications. E.g., in robot navigation, over multiple episodes (interaction trials with the environment), a robot needs to learn an optimal route to the final destination, as shown in Fig. <a href="#S2.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 2.1 Finite-horizon episodic MDP under distribution shifts ‣ 2 Preliminary" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. There are slippery sections on the route that may cause the robot to move in an undesirable direction. Over time, the environment, i.e., the slippery levels, can change across episodes due to weather conditions. Because of this distribution shift, the optimal policy can change (e.g., route A with more slippery than B, now becomes less slippery than B). As not designed to handle this kind of shift, QUCB with non-shift-aware ability, may exploit sub-optimal reward by an old policy (learned policy before the shift), resulting in a bad performance after the shift occurs.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To address the non-shift-aware issue in QUCB, we introduce Density-QUCB (DQUCB), a shift-aware Q-learning UCB algorithm, which uses a transition density function to adjust the exploration rate of the UCB term. The key idea of our method is leveraging the likelihood of this density function as an out-of-distribution detector, i.e., when there is no shift, its likelihood will be high, and our model will be more certain (exploitation). In contrast, its likelihood will be low when the distribution shift occurs, which means our model will be more uncertain (exploration). This helps our model improve UCB uncertainty quantification, be able to explore new policies, and avoid exploiting an old policy when the shift happens, resulting in a better regret guarantee than the non-shift-aware QUCB algorithm.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Our contributions are outlined in Tab. <a href="#S1.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 1 Introduction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and as follows:</p>
<ul id="S1.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="S1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We propose DQUCB, a shift-aware Q-learning UCB algorithm to enhance the uncertainty quantification quality of UCB with Q-learning, resulting in a balance between exploration and exploitation in the non-stationary RL under distribution shifts.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We theoretically prove the regret of our DQUCB algorithm in the finite-horizon episodic MDP is at most <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}\left(\sqrt{H^{5}(1+\epsilon)^{2}|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|K\log(|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|KH/\delta)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}\left(\sqrt{H^{5}(1+\epsilon)^{2}|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|K\log(|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|KH/\delta)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{S}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{S}|</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{A}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{A}|</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> are the number of state, action, planning horizon, episodes, and density estimator error, correspondingly. And in infinite-horizon discounted MDP is at most <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|(1+\epsilon)}{(1-\gamma)^{6}\min\{\Delta_{\min},\bar{\Delta}_{\min}\}}\log\left(\frac{|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|T}{(1-\gamma)\min\{\Delta_{\min},\bar{\Delta}_{\min}\}}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>6</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>min</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>min</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|(1+\epsilon)}{(1-\gamma)^{6}\min\{\Delta_{\min},\bar{\Delta}_{\min}\}}\log\left(\frac{|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|T}{(1-\gamma)\min\{\Delta_{\min},\bar{\Delta}_{\min}\}}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is the discount factor, <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of cumulative steps, and <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\min},\bar{\Delta}_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\min},\bar{\Delta}_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> are the minimum sub-optimality gap. Notably, our oracle DQUCB algorithm (i.e., when <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>) is strictly better than the non-shift-aware version (i.e., QUCB) in both finite-horizon episodic and infinite-horizon discounted MDP settings.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We empirically show DQUCB outperforms QUCB by achieving lower regret on GridWorld and Frozen-Lake. In addition, it exhibits the computational efficiency of model-free RL and outperforms model-based RL (e.g., UCBVI, UCBMQ) in space and time complexity (see Fig. <a href="#S5.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 5.2 Main results ‣ 5 Experiments" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>). Furthermore, we extend this framework to neural-network versions on CartPole, COVID-19 patient hospital allocation task, and show it consistently achieves a lower cumulative regret than other Deep Q-learning baselines.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Preliminary</h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper, we consider two RL settings in an unknown MDP, including when the learning agent interacts with the system with (i.e., finite-horizon episodic MDP) and without (i.e., infinite-horizon discounted MDP) any reset. For simplicity, our formal setting considers one time shift. Our results can also be extended to multiple time shifts using our general proof techniques or a similar analysis. We formally define these settings under distribution shifts as follows:</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.1 </span>Finite-horizon episodic MDP under distribution shifts</h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the first setting, an episodic Markov Decision Process (MDP) is a tuple <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}:=\langle\mathcal{S},\mathcal{A},H,\mathbb{P},r\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}:=\langle\mathcal{S},\mathcal{A},H,\mathbb{P},r\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is the state space, <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is the action space, <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> is the planning horizon, <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{h}:\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}\rightarrow\Delta(\mathcal{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{h}:\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}\rightarrow\Delta(\mathcal{S})</annotation></semantics></math> is the transition operator at step <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> that takes a state-action pair and returns a distribution over states, and <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{h}:\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}\rightarrow[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{h}:\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}\rightarrow[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> is the
deterministic reward function at step <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>. For a finite-horizon episodic MDP, the agent interacts with the MDP for <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> episodes. For each episode <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[K]</annotation></semantics></math>, the agent starts at an initial state <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{1}\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1}\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> picked by an adversary <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jin et al., 2018</a>; <a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Menard et al., 2021</a>)</cite>. In this setting, we focus on the distribution shift of the transition operator <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> at a particular episode <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{K}\in[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{K}\in[K]</annotation></semantics></math>. Let us denote <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mathbb{P}}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathbb{P}}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> as the transition operator after the distribution shift occurs. Hence, <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{s}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{s}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> means the state r.v. sampled from <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mathbb{P}}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathbb{P}}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>. Given a policy <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> which is a sequence of mappings <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{h}:\mathcal{S}\rightarrow\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{h}:\mathcal{S}\rightarrow\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math>, for a state <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, the value function of state <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> at the <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>-step are defined as</p>
<table id="S2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{h}^{\pi}(s):=\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{h^{\prime}=h}^{H}r_{h^{\prime}}(s_{h^{\prime}},\pi_{h^{\prime}}(s_{h^{\prime}}))\Big|s_{h}=s\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{h}^{\pi}(s):=\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{h^{\prime}=h}^{H}r_{h^{\prime}}(s_{h^{\prime}},\pi_{h^{\prime}}(s_{h^{\prime}}))\Big|s_{h}=s\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\bar{V}_{h}^{\pi}(s):=\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{h^{\prime}=h}^{H}r_{h^{\prime}}(\bar{s}_{h^{\prime}},\pi_{h^{\prime}}(\bar{s}_{h^{\prime}}))\Big|\bar{s}_{h}=s\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\bar{V}_{h}^{\pi}(s):=\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{h^{\prime}=h}^{H}r_{h^{\prime}}(\bar{s}_{h^{\prime}},\pi_{h^{\prime}}(\bar{s}_{h^{\prime}}))\Big|\bar{s}_{h}=s\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and the associated <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>-function of a state-action pair <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,a)\in\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,a)\in\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> at the <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>-step are <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m26" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Q_{h}^{\pi}(s,a):=r_{h}(s,a)+\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{h^{\prime}=h+1}^{H}r_{h^{\prime}}(s_{h^{\prime}},\pi_{h^{\prime}}(s_{h^{\prime}}))\Big|s_{h}=s,a_{h}=a\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>H</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>r</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{h}^{\pi}(s,a):=r_{h}(s,a)+\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{h^{\prime}=h+1}^{H}r_{h^{\prime}}(s_{h^{\prime}},\pi_{h^{\prime}}(s_{h^{\prime}}))\Big|s_{h}=s,a_{h}=a\right]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m27" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bar{Q}_{h}^{\pi}(s,a):=r_{h}(s,a)+\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{h^{\prime}=h+1}^{H}r_{h^{\prime}}(\bar{s}_{h^{\prime}},\pi_{h^{\prime}}(\bar{s}_{h^{\prime}}))\Big|\bar{s}_{h}=s,a_{h}=a\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>H</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>r</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{Q}_{h}^{\pi}(s,a):=r_{h}(s,a)+\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{h^{\prime}=h+1}^{H}r_{h^{\prime}}(\bar{s}_{h^{\prime}},\pi_{h^{\prime}}(\bar{s}_{h^{\prime}}))\Big|\bar{s}_{h}=s,a_{h}=a\right]</annotation></semantics></math>.
We let <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\pi}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\pi}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> be the optimal policy s.t. <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\pi^{*}}(s)=V^{*}(s)=\sup_{\pi}V^{\pi}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mi>π</mi></msub><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\pi^{*}}(s)=V^{*}(s)=\sup_{\pi}V^{\pi}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{V}^{\bar{\pi}^{*}}(s)=\bar{V}^{*}(s)=\sup_{\pi}\bar{V}^{\pi}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mi>π</mi></msub><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{V}^{\bar{\pi}^{*}}(s)=\bar{V}^{*}(s)=\sup_{\pi}\bar{V}^{\pi}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{*}(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{*}(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{Q}^{*}(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{Q}^{*}(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math> mean the Q-function under optimal policy <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\pi}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\pi}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. respectively, <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∀</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math>. For each episode <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[K]</annotation></semantics></math>, the learning agent specifies a policy <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, plays <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> steps and observes trajectory <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s_{1},a_{1}),\cdots,(s_{H},a_{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s_{1},a_{1}),\cdots,(s_{H},a_{H})</annotation></semantics></math>. The total number of steps is <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="KH" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">KH</annotation></semantics></math>, and the total (expected) regret of an execution instance of the agent is then</p>
<table id="S2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Regret}(K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Regret</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Regret}(K)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\sum_{k=1}^{\bar{K}}(V_{1}^{*}-V_{1}^{\pi_{k}})(s_{1}^{k})+\sum_{k=\bar{K}+1}^{K}(\bar{V}_{1}^{*}-\bar{V}_{1}^{\pi_{k}})(s_{1}^{k})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\sum_{k=1}^{\bar{K}}(V_{1}^{*}-V_{1}^{\pi_{k}})(s_{1}^{k})+\sum_{k=\bar{K}+1}^{K}(\bar{V}_{1}^{*}-\bar{V}_{1}^{\pi_{k}})(s_{1}^{k}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<figure id="S2.F1" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.03181v1/setting.svg" id="S2.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:673/316;" width="673" height="316"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span>Robot navigation example, where <math id="S2.F1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the set of slippery distributions on the route <math id="S2.F1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbb{P}_{h}\}_{h\in[H]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbb{P}_{h}\}_{h\in[H]}</annotation></semantics></math> at episode k-th. We consider a more general case of prior works. Specifically, prior works set <math id="S2.F1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbb{P}_{h}\}_{h\in[H]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbb{P}_{h}\}_{h\in[H]}</annotation></semantics></math> stay the same over episode <math id="S2.F1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[K]</annotation></semantics></math>, we consider <math id="S2.F1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbb{P}_{h}\}_{h\in[H]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbb{P}_{h}\}_{h\in[H]}</annotation></semantics></math> can change across different episodes <math id="S2.F1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[K]</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, in the infinite-horizon discounted MDP, prior works consider a fixed <math id="S2.F1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℙ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}</annotation></semantics></math> across time steps, while we consider that <math id="S2.F1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℙ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}</annotation></semantics></math> can change.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">It is worth noting that we consider a general case, rather than a special case of the literature on a non-stationary MDP <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jin et al., 2018</a>; <a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Menard et al., 2021</a>)</cite>. Specifically, prior works consider the case of transition functions <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> changing across the time horizon <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math> within an episode, i.e., <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is different over <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math> but the set <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbb{P}_{h}\}_{h\in[H]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbb{P}_{h}\}_{h\in[H]}</annotation></semantics></math> stay the same over episode <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[K]</annotation></semantics></math>. Meanwhile, our method considers that the transition functions additionally change across episodes, i.e., <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> differs over <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math> and the set <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbb{P}_{h}\}_{h\in[H]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbb{P}_{h}\}_{h\in[H]}</annotation></semantics></math> can also change across different episodes <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[K]</annotation></semantics></math> (see Fig. <a href="#S2.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 2.1 Finite-horizon episodic MDP under distribution shifts ‣ 2 Preliminary" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.2 </span>Infinite-horizon discounted MDP under distribution shifts</h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the second setting, we consider a tuple <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\gamma}:=\langle\mathcal{S},\mathcal{A},\gamma,\mathbb{P},r\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\gamma}:=\langle\mathcal{S},\mathcal{A},\gamma,\mathbb{P},r\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is the discount factor, <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℙ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}</annotation></semantics></math> is the transition operator, and <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> is the reward function <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2020</a>; <a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2021</a>)</cite>. We focus on the distribution shift of the transition operator <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℙ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}</annotation></semantics></math> at a particular time step <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{T}\in[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{T}\in[T]</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of first time steps. Let us denote <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mathbb{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathbb{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> as the transition operator after the distribution shift occurs. Hence, <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{s}</annotation></semantics></math> means the state r.v. sampled from <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mathbb{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathbb{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}:=\{\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}\times[0,1]\}^{*}\times\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}:=\{\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}\times[0,1]\}^{*}\times\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of all possible trajectories of any length. A non-stationary deterministic policy <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:\mathcal{C}\rightarrow\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:\mathcal{C}\rightarrow\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is a mapping from paths to actions. The <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> function and <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> function are defined as follows</p>
<table id="S2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V^{\pi}(s):=\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}\gamma^{i-1}r(s_{i},\pi(c_{i}))\Big|s_{1}=s\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V^{\pi}(s):=\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}\gamma^{i-1}r(s_{i},\pi(c_{i}))\Big|s_{1}=s\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\bar{V}^{\pi}(s):=\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}\gamma^{i-1}r(\bar{s}_{i},\pi(\bar{c}_{i}))\Big|\bar{s}_{1}=s\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\bar{V}^{\pi}(s):=\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}\gamma^{i-1}r(\bar{s}_{i},\pi(\bar{c}_{i}))\Big|\bar{s}_{1}=s\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Q^{\pi}(s,a):=r(s,a)+\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{i=2}^{\infty}\gamma^{i-1}r(s_{i},\pi(c_{i}))\Big|s_{1}=s,a_{1}=a\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\pi}(s,a):=r(s,a)+\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{i=2}^{\infty}\gamma^{i-1}r(s_{i},\pi(c_{i}))\Big|s_{1}=s,a_{1}=a\right]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bar{Q}^{\pi}(s,a):=r(s,a)+\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{i=2}^{\infty}\gamma^{i-1}r(\bar{s}_{i},\pi(\bar{c}_{i}))\Big|\bar{s}_{1}=s,a_{1}=a\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{Q}^{\pi}(s,a):=r(s,a)+\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{i=2}^{\infty}\gamma^{i-1}r(\bar{s}_{i},\pi(\bar{c}_{i}))\Big|\bar{s}_{1}=s,a_{1}=a\right]</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(c_{i}:=(s_{1},\pi(s_{1}),r(s_{1},\pi(s_{1})),\cdots,s_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(c_{i}:=(s_{1},\pi(s_{1}),r(s_{1},\pi(s_{1})),\cdots,s_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bar{c}_{i}:=(\bar{s}_{1},\pi(\bar{s}_{1}),r(\bar{s}_{1},\pi(\bar{s}_{1})),\cdots,\bar{s}_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bar{c}_{i}:=(\bar{s}_{1},\pi(\bar{s}_{1}),r(\bar{s}_{1},\pi(\bar{s}_{1})),\cdots,\bar{s}_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider the interaction with the environment that starts at state <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, a learning agent specifies an initial non-stationary policy <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. At each time step <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the agent takes action <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t}(s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t}(s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, observe <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and updates <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. The total regret of the agent for the first <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> steps is thus defined as</p>
<table id="S2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Regert}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Regert</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Regert}(T)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\sum_{t=1}^{\bar{T}}(V^{*}-V^{\pi_{t}})(s_{t})+\sum_{t=\bar{T}+1}^{T}(\bar{V}^{*}-\bar{V}^{\pi_{t}})(s_{t})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\sum_{t=1}^{\bar{T}}(V^{*}-V^{\pi_{t}})(s_{t})+\sum_{t=\bar{T}+1}^{T}(\bar{V}^{*}-\bar{V}^{\pi_{t}})(s_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">It is worth noting that while <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. (2020)</a></cite> considers a fixed transition function <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℙ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}</annotation></semantics></math> across time steps, we consider a more general case by <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℙ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}</annotation></semantics></math> can change at a particular time step <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[T]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Shift-Aware Density Q-Learning UCB</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To handle the aforementioned settings, based on Q-learning, we next introduce our main methodology.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F2" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.03181v1/RLframework.svg" id="S3.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:673/244;" width="673" height="244"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>Our shift-aware Q-learning UCB can be more uncertain (i.e., more exploration) if the environment changes because of a low likelihood from <math id="S3.F2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(\cdot|s,a;\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\cdot|s,a;\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>, and more certain (i.e., more exploitation) if the environment stays the same because of a high likelihood from <math id="S3.F2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(\cdot|s,a;\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\cdot|s,a;\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">In the finite-horizon episodic MDP</span>, our Alg. <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3 Shift-Aware Density Q-Learning UCB" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> maintains <math id="S3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> values, <math id="S3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{h}(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{h}(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="S3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,a,h)\in\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}\times[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,a,h)\in\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}\times[H]</annotation></semantics></math> and the corresponding <math id="S3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> value, i.e.,</p>
<table id="S3.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{h}(s)\leftarrow\min\{H,\max_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}}Q_{h}(s,a^{\prime})\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{h}(s)\leftarrow\min\{H,\max_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}}Q_{h}(s,a^{\prime})\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">If at time step <math id="S3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math>, the state is <math id="S3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and the algorithm takes action <math id="S3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> that maximizes the current estimate <math id="S3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{h}(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{h}(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math>, and is apprised of the next state <math id="S3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>. The algorithm then updates the <math id="S3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> values by</p>
<table id="S3.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{h}(s,a)\leftarrow(1-\alpha_{t})Q_{h}(s,a)+\alpha_{t}[r_{h}(s,a)+V_{h+1}(s^{\prime})+b_{t}]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{h}(s,a)\leftarrow(1-\alpha_{t})Q_{h}(s,a)+\alpha_{t}[r_{h}(s,a)+V_{h+1}(s^{\prime})+b_{t}],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=N_{h}(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=N_{h}(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of times the algorithm has visited the state-action pair <math id="S3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the learning rate, and <math id="S3.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the confidence value indicating how certain the algorithm is about the current state-action pair, and are defined as follows</p>
<table id="S3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha_{t}:=\frac{H+1}{H+t},\quad b_{t}:=\frac{c}{p(s_{h+1}|s_{h},a_{h};\theta_{h})}\sqrt{H^{3}\iota/t}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ι</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha_{t}:=\frac{H+1}{H+t},\quad b_{t}:=\frac{c}{p(s_{h+1}|s_{h},a_{h};\theta_{h})}\sqrt{H^{3}\iota/t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota=\log(|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|KH/\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ι</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota=\log(|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|KH/\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(s_{h+1}|s_{h},a_{h};\theta_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(s_{h+1}|s_{h},a_{h};\theta_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> is the likelihood value of density function <math id="S3.p2.m18" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(\cdot|s,a;\theta_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\cdot|s,a;\theta_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> parameterized by parameter <math id="S3.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, at state <math id="S3.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{h+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{h+1}</annotation></semantics></math> condition on previous state-action <math id="S3.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s_{h},a_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s_{h},a_{h})</annotation></semantics></math>, and is computed following Bayes’s rule as follows</p>
<table id="S3.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(s_{h+1}|s_{h},a_{h};\theta_{h})=\frac{p(s_{h+1},s_{h},a_{h};\theta_{h})}{p(s_{h},a_{h};\theta_{h})}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(s_{h+1}|s_{h},a_{h};\theta_{h})=\frac{p(s_{h+1},s_{h},a_{h};\theta_{h})}{p(s_{h},a_{h};\theta_{h})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.5" class="ltx_p">where parameter <math id="S3.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is updated by using maximum likelihood estimation with <math id="S3.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> most recent tuples <math id="S3.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s^{\prime},s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s^{\prime},s,a)</annotation></semantics></math> from the interaction with the environment. Specifically about our density function <math id="S3.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(s^{\prime}|s,a;\theta_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(s^{\prime}|s,a;\theta_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> above, we use <math id="S3.p2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(s^{\prime}|s,a;\theta_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(s^{\prime}|s,a;\theta_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> to estimate the likelihood of sample <math id="S3.p2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s^{\prime},s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s^{\prime},s,a)</annotation></semantics></math> from the probability density ratio, i.e., <math id="S3.p2.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(s^{\prime}|s,a;\theta_{h})\approx f_{X}(s^{\prime}|s,a)/f_{Y}(s^{\prime}|s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(s^{\prime}|s,a;\theta_{h})\approx f_{X}(s^{\prime}|s,a)/f_{Y}(s^{\prime}|s,a)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.p2.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s^{\prime},s,a)\sim\mathbb{P}_{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s^{\prime},s,a)\sim\mathbb{P}_{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p2.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{h}=\arg\max_{\theta_{h}}p(D_{n}|\theta_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{h}=\arg\max_{\theta_{h}}p(D_{n}|\theta_{h})</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S3.p2.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}\sim\mathbb{P}_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}\sim\mathbb{P}_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> is the cumulative dataset with <math id="S3.p2.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> data points. When before the shift, <math id="S3.p2.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s^{\prime},s,a)\sim\mathbb{P}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s^{\prime},s,a)\sim\mathbb{P}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p2.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}\sim\mathbb{P}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}\sim\mathbb{P}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, thus <math id="S3.p2.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{X}=\mathbb{P}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{X}=\mathbb{P}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p2.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{Y}=\mathbb{P}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{Y}=\mathbb{P}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>. When the shift occurs at episode <math id="S3.p2.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p2.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s^{\prime},s,a)\sim\bar{\mathbb{P}}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s^{\prime},s,a)\sim\bar{\mathbb{P}}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and the cumulative dataset <math id="S3.p2.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}\sim\mathbb{P}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}\sim\mathbb{P}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, thus <math id="S3.p2.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{X}=\mathbb{P}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{X}=\mathbb{P}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p2.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{Y}=\bar{\mathbb{P}}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{Y}=\bar{\mathbb{P}}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>. After episode <math id="S3.p2.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, the cumulative dataset accumulates data from the new distribution, i.e., <math id="S3.p2.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}\sim\bar{\mathbb{P}}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}\sim\bar{\mathbb{P}}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence for <math id="S3.p2.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s^{\prime},s,a)\sim\bar{\mathbb{P}}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s^{\prime},s,a)\sim\bar{\mathbb{P}}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S3.p2.m45" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{X}=\bar{\mathbb{P}}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{X}=\bar{\mathbb{P}}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p2.m46" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{Y}=\bar{\mathbb{P}}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{Y}=\bar{\mathbb{P}}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">From the uncertainty term <math id="S3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. <a href="#S3.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ 3 Shift-Aware Density Q-Learning UCB" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, we can see that while <math id="S3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is monotonically increasing, <math id="S3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(s_{h+1}|s_{h},a_{h};\theta_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(s_{h+1}|s_{h},a_{h};\theta_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> is initialized to estimate the density of <math id="S3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s^{\prime},s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s^{\prime},s,a)</annotation></semantics></math> sampled from transition operator <math id="S3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, over time, the likelihood <math id="S3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(s_{h+1}|s_{h},a_{h};\theta_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(s_{h+1}|s_{h},a_{h};\theta_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> will be high, yielding the exploration rate in <math id="S3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to be low, i.e., the algorithm will be more certain (i.e., exploitation) about its prediction from the mean <math id="S3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{h}(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{h}(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math>. When the shift happens at episode <math id="S3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(s_{h+1}|s_{h},a_{h};\theta_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(s_{h+1}|s_{h},a_{h};\theta_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> behaves as an out-of-distriubiton detector because its likelihood will measure the ratio of <math id="S3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{h}/\bar{\mathbb{P}}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{h}/\bar{\mathbb{P}}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, decreasing value, yielding the exploration rate in <math id="S3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> will be high, i.e., the algorithm will be more uncertain (i.e., exploration) about its prediction from the mean <math id="S3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{h}(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{h}(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math>. We show this key idea in Fig. <a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 3 Shift-Aware Density Q-Learning UCB" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Comparison with model-based RL</span>. It is worth noticing that although our function <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(\cdot|s,a;\theta_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\cdot|s,a;\theta_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> estimates the density of samples from the transition function, it does not explicitly model the transition operator <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> like the model-based method (e.g., UCBVI, UCBMQ, etc.), which needs to store and iterate through all possible <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s^{\prime},s,a)\in\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s^{\prime},s,a)\in\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> tuples with <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{O}}(KH\mathcal{|}S|^{2}|\mathcal{A}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{O}}(KH\mathcal{|}S|^{2}|\mathcal{A}|)</annotation></semantics></math> time complexity and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{S}|^{2}|\mathcal{A}|H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{S}|^{2}|\mathcal{A}|H)</annotation></semantics></math> space complexity <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Auer et al., 2008</a>)</cite>. Indeed, our training step for <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(\cdot|s,a;\theta_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\cdot|s,a;\theta_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> only depends on the number of cumulative observed <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s^{\prime},s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s^{\prime},s,a)</annotation></semantics></math> tuples with <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> window-size. In general, <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(\cdot|s,a;\theta_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\cdot|s,a;\theta_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> can be any density function. In our experiment, we use Kernel Density Estimation (KDE). Therefore, the time complexity of our DQUCB algorithm is <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(KHn^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(KHn^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|Hn)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|Hn)</annotation></semantics></math>, which is much computationally efficient than model-based baselines (e.g., Fig. <a href="#S5.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 5.2 Main results ‣ 5 Experiments" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>). Note that we can also further improve our algorithm’s complexity by applying other density estimation techniques that have near-linear time and space complexity <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chan et al., 2014</a>; <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bousquet et al., 2019</a>; <a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Backurs et al., 2019</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_figure ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Our DQUCB algorithm in the finite-horizon episodic MDP</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_align_center ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Initialize</span> <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{h}(s,a)\leftarrow H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{h}(s,a)\leftarrow H</annotation></semantics></math> &amp; <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{h}(s,a)\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{h}(s,a)\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall(s,a,h)\in\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}\times[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∀</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall(s,a,h)\in\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}\times[H]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\cdot;\theta_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\cdot;\theta_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}=\frac{H+1}{H+t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}=\frac{H+1}{H+t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota=\log(|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|KH/\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ι</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota=\log(|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|KH/\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> every episode <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[K]</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
            Receive <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> step <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
             Take <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{h}\leftarrow\arg\max_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}}Q_{h}(s_{h},a^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{h}\leftarrow\arg\max_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}}Q_{h}(s_{h},a^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, observe <math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{h+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{h+1}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=N_{h}(s_{h},a_{h})\leftarrow N_{h}(s_{h},a_{h})+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=N_{h}(s_{h},a_{h})\leftarrow N_{h}(s_{h},a_{h})+1</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t}\leftarrow\frac{c}{p(s_{h+1}|s_{h},a_{h};\theta_{h})}\sqrt{H^{3}\iota/t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ι</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t}\leftarrow\frac{c}{p(s_{h+1}|s_{h},a_{h};\theta_{h})}\sqrt{H^{3}\iota/t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{h}(s_{h},a_{h})\leftarrow(1-\alpha_{t})Q_{h}(s_{h},a_{h})+\alpha_{t}\left[r_{h}(s_{h},a_{h})+V_{h+1}(s_{h+1})+b_{t}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{h}(s_{h},a_{h})\leftarrow(1-\alpha_{t})Q_{h}(s_{h},a_{h})+\alpha_{t}\left[r_{h}(s_{h},a_{h})+V_{h+1}(s_{h+1})+b_{t}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{h}(s_{h})\leftarrow\min\{H,\max_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}}Q_{h}(s_{h},a^{\prime})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{h}(s_{h})\leftarrow\min\{H,\max_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}}Q_{h}(s_{h},a^{\prime})\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            
             Update <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> of model <math id="alg1.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\cdot;\theta_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\cdot;\theta_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="alg1.l10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(s_{h+1}|s_{h},a_{h};\theta_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(s_{h+1}|s_{h},a_{h};\theta_{h})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="S3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">In the infinite-horizon discounted MDP</span>, our Alg. <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ 3 Shift-Aware Density Q-Learning UCB" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> maintains <math id="S3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> values, <math id="S3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="S3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,a)\in\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,a)\in\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and the corresponding <math id="S3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{V}</annotation></semantics></math> value, i.e.,</p>
<table id="S3.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{V}(s_{t+1})\leftarrow\max_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}}\hat{Q}(s_{t+1},a^{\prime})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{V}(s_{t+1})\leftarrow\max_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}}\hat{Q}(s_{t+1},a^{\prime}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{Q}(s_{t},a_{t})\leftarrow\min\left\{\hat{Q}(s_{t},a_{t}),Q(s_{t},a_{t})\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{Q}(s_{t},a_{t})\leftarrow\min\left\{\hat{Q}(s_{t},a_{t}),Q(s_{t},a_{t})\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">If, at time step <math id="S3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[T]</annotation></semantics></math>, the state is <math id="S3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, the algorithm takes the action <math id="S3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> that maximizes the current estimate <math id="S3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math>, and is apprised of the next sate <math id="S3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>. The algorithm then updates the <math id="S3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> values as follows</p>
<table id="S3.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q(s_{t},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q(s_{t},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leftarrow(1-\alpha_{k})Q(s_{t},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leftarrow(1-\alpha_{k})Q(s_{t},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\alpha_{k}\left[r(s_{t},a_{t})+\gamma\hat{V}(s_{t+1})+b_{k}\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\alpha_{k}\left[r(s_{t},a_{t})+\gamma\hat{V}(s_{t+1})+b_{k}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p4.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=N(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=N(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of times the algorithm has visited the state-action pair <math id="S3.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the learning rate, and <math id="S3.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the confidence value indicating how certain the algorithm is about the current state-action pair, and are defined as follows</p>
<table id="S3.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha_{k}:=\frac{H+1}{H+k},b_{k}:=\frac{c_{2}}{(1-\gamma)p(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t};\theta)}\sqrt{H\iota(k)/k}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ι</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha_{k}:=\frac{H+1}{H+k},b_{k}:=\frac{c_{2}}{(1-\gamma)p(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t};\theta)}\sqrt{H\iota(k)/k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p4.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\leftarrow\frac{\ln(2/(1-\gamma))}{\ln(1/\gamma)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\leftarrow\frac{\ln(2/(1-\gamma))}{\ln(1/\gamma)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota(k)=\log(|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|T(k+1)(k+2))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ι</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota(k)=\log(|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|T(k+1)(k+2))</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t};\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t};\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is the likelihood value of density function <math id="S3.p4.m18" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(\cdot|s,a;\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\cdot|s,a;\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> at state <math id="S3.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> condition on previous state-action <math id="S3.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s_{t},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s_{t},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, and is computed following Bayes’s rule as follows</p>
<table id="S3.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t};\theta)=\frac{p(s_{t+1},s_{t},a_{t};\theta)}{p(s_{t},a_{t};\theta)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t};\theta)=\frac{p(s_{t+1},s_{t},a_{t};\theta)}{p(s_{t},a_{t};\theta)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p4.5" class="ltx_p">where parameter <math id="S3.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> is updated by <math id="S3.p4.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> most recent tuples <math id="S3.p4.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s^{\prime},s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s^{\prime},s,a)</annotation></semantics></math>. From the uncertainty term <math id="S3.p4.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. <a href="#S3.E11" title="Equation 11 ‣ 3 Shift-Aware Density Q-Learning UCB" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>, we can see that while <math id="S3.p4.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is monotonically increasing, <math id="S3.p4.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t};\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t};\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is initialized to estimate the density of <math id="S3.p4.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s^{\prime},s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s^{\prime},s,a)</annotation></semantics></math> sampled from transition operator <math id="S3.p4.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℙ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}</annotation></semantics></math>, over time, the likelihood <math id="S3.p4.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t};\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t};\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> will be high, yielding the exploration rate in <math id="S3.p4.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> will be low, i.e., the algorithm will be more certain (i.e., exploitation). When the shift happens at time step <math id="S3.p4.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p4.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t};\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t};\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> behaves as a out-of-distriubiton detector by its likelihood will measure the ratio of <math id="S3.p4.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}/\bar{\mathbb{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>/</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}/\bar{\mathbb{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>, decreasing value, yielding the exploration rate in <math id="S3.p4.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> will be high, i.e., the algorithm will be more uncertain (i.e., exploration).</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_figure ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Our DQUCB algorithm in the infinite-horizon discounted MDP</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_align_center ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg2.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Initialize</span> <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(s,a)\leftarrow\frac{1}{1-\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(s,a)\leftarrow\frac{1}{1-\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> &amp; <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(s,a)\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(s,a)\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall(s,a)\in\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∀</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall(s,a)\in\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\cdot;\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\cdot;\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{k}=\frac{H+1}{H+k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{k}=\frac{H+1}{H+k}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota(k)=\log(|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|T(k+1)(k+2))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ι</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota(k)=\log(|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|T(k+1)(k+2))</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\leftarrow\frac{\ln(2/(1-\gamma))}{\ln(1/\gamma)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\leftarrow\frac{\ln(2/(1-\gamma))}{\ln(1/\gamma)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg2.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> every step <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[T]</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
            Take <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}\leftarrow\arg\max_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}}Q(s_{t},a^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}\leftarrow\arg\max_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}}Q(s_{t},a^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, observe <math id="alg2.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=N(s_{t},a_{t})\leftarrow N(s_{t},a_{t})+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=N(s_{t},a_{t})\leftarrow N(s_{t},a_{t})+1</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{k}\leftarrow\frac{c_{2}}{(1-\gamma)p(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t};\theta)}\sqrt{H\iota(k)/k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ι</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{k}\leftarrow\frac{c_{2}}{(1-\gamma)p(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t};\theta)}\sqrt{H\iota(k)/k}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{V}(s_{t+1})\leftarrow\max_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}}\hat{Q}(s_{t+1},a^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{V}(s_{t+1})\leftarrow\max_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}}\hat{Q}(s_{t+1},a^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(s_{t},a_{t})\leftarrow(1-\alpha_{k})Q(s_{t},a_{t})+\alpha_{k}\left[r(s_{t},a_{t})+\gamma\hat{V}(s_{t+1})+b_{k}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(s_{t},a_{t})\leftarrow(1-\alpha_{k})Q(s_{t},a_{t})+\alpha_{k}\left[r(s_{t},a_{t})+\gamma\hat{V}(s_{t+1})+b_{k}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{Q}(s_{t},a_{t})\leftarrow\min\left\{\hat{Q}(s_{t},a_{t}),Q(s_{t},a_{t})\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{Q}(s_{t},a_{t})\leftarrow\min\left\{\hat{Q}(s_{t},a_{t}),Q(s_{t},a_{t})\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
            Update <math id="alg2.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> of model <math id="alg2.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\cdot;\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\cdot;\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="alg2.l9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t};\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t};\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg2.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Theoretical analysis</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To formally explain why our shift-aware DQUCB can improve the uncertainty estimation quality of UCB with Q-learning, resulting in a balance between exploration and exploitation under distribution shifts, we next analyze the cumulative regret of Alg. <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3 Shift-Aware Density Q-Learning UCB" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and Alg. <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ 3 Shift-Aware Density Q-Learning UCB" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. We first provide the regret bound for the Alg. <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3 Shift-Aware Density Q-Learning UCB" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> in the finite-horizon episodic MDP under distribution shifts:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4.1</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists an absolute constant <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, if we choose <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t}=\frac{c}{p(\cdot|s,a;\theta_{h})}\sqrt{H^{3}\iota/t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ι</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t}=\frac{c}{p(\cdot|s,a;\theta_{h})}\sqrt{H^{3}\iota/t}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=N_{h}(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=N_{h}(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math>, then with probability <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, the regret of the Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3 Shift-Aware Density Q-Learning UCB" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Regret}(K)\leq\mathcal{O}\left(\sqrt{H^{5}(1+\epsilon)^{2}|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|K\log(|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|KH/\delta)}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Regret</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Regret}(K)\leq\mathcal{O}\left(\sqrt{H^{5}(1+\epsilon)^{2}|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|K\log(|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|KH/\delta)}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is the estimator error of <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1/p(\cdot|s,a;\theta_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/p(\cdot|s,a;\theta_{h})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 4.2</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Thm. <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4 Theoretical analysis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> shows that when the estimation error <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>, our DQUCB in Alg. <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3 Shift-Aware Density Q-Learning UCB" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> achieves <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}\left(\sqrt{H^{5}|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|K\log(|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|KH/\delta)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}\left(\sqrt{H^{5}|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|K\log(|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|KH/\delta)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>regret bound. Meanwhile, due to the distribution shift, the non-shift-aware version, i.e., Q-learning Hoeffding UCB <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jin et al., 2018</a>)</cite> with the selection of <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{k}=c\sqrt{H^{3}\iota/t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ι</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{k}=c\sqrt{H^{3}\iota/t}</annotation></semantics></math>, can leads to <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}\left(\sqrt{H^{5}|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|\bar{K}\log(|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|\bar{K}H/\delta)}+H(K-\bar{K})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}\left(\sqrt{H^{5}|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|\bar{K}\log(|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|\bar{K}H/\delta)}+H(K-\bar{K})\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{K\rightarrow\infty}\frac{\sqrt{H^{5}|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|K\log(|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|KH/\delta)}}{\sqrt{H^{5}|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|\bar{K}\log(|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|\bar{K}H/\delta)}+H(K-\bar{K})}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{K\rightarrow\infty}\frac{\sqrt{H^{5}|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|K\log(|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|KH/\delta)}}{\sqrt{H^{5}|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|\bar{K}\log(|\mathcal{S}||\mathcal{A}|\bar{K}H/\delta)}+H(K-\bar{K})}=0</annotation></semantics></math> by L’Hôpital’s rule, we can see that the regret bound of our shift-aware DQUCB in Alg. <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3 Shift-Aware Density Q-Learning UCB" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> when <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>, is strictly better than the non-shift-aware version QUCB.</p>
</div>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F3" class="ltx_figure">
<table id="S4.F3.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
