<td id="A2.F7.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:0.1pt;padding-right:0.1pt;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.03181v1/frozen_lake.svg" id="A2.F7.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:202/204;" width="202" height="204"></object></td>
<td id="A2.F7.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:0.1pt;padding-right:0.1pt;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.03181v1/cartpole.svg" id="A2.F7.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:236/179;" width="236" height="179"></object></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.F7.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.F7.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:0.1pt;padding-right:0.1pt;">(a)</td>
<td id="A2.F7.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:0.1pt;padding-right:0.1pt;">(b)</td>
<td id="A2.F7.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:0.1pt;padding-right:0.1pt;">(c)</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>(a) The GridWorld task: the starting state is shown in red, the rewarding state is shown in yellow, and the transitions are noisy with <math id="A2.F7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>; (b) The Frozen-Lake task: the starting state is the chair at the top-left corner, the rewarding state is the box at the bottom-right corner, the goal is crossing a frozen lake from start to the rewarding state without falling into any holes by walking over the frozen lake, and the transitions are noisy with a slippery level <math id="A2.F7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>; (c) The CartPole task: the pendulum is placed upright on the cart, the goal is to balance the pole, and the transition noise <math id="A2.F7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(0,0.15)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.15</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(0,0.15)</annotation></semantics></math> is added to the velocity state.</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Experimental settings</h3>

<section id="A2.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.1.1 </span>GridWorld</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fig. <a href="#A2.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Appendix B Experimental details" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> (a) shows our <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[10]\times[5]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>10</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[10]\times[5]</annotation></semantics></math> GridWorld environment with <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math> states and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> actions (left, right, up, down). When the agent uses its policy to take action, it will move in the corresponding direction following the action with probability <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, and move to a neighbor state at random with probability <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. The starting position is <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. The reward is equal to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> in state <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(10,5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(10,5)</annotation></semantics></math> and is zero elsewhere. We set the planning horizon <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=100</annotation></semantics></math> and the number of episodes <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=50000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=50000</annotation></semantics></math>. From the first episode to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{K}=25000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>25000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{K}=25000</annotation></semantics></math>, the noise is <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>. After that, the transition function is shifted by changing <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=0.2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">State</span>: The state <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}=(i,j)\in[10]\times[5]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>10</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}=(i,j)\in[10]\times[5]</annotation></semantics></math> at step <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> consists of the agent’s position on the grid, where <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is the row and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> is the column index. <span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Action</span>: Action <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}\in\{left,right,up,down\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}\in\{left,right,up,down\}</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is the direction in which the agent will try to reach. <span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">State Transition Function</span>: From position state <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the next position of agent <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> will follow action <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> with probability <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, and move to a random neighbor position of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> with probability <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. <span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reward Function</span>: The reward <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> equals <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> when the agent reaches the final state <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(10,5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(10,5)</annotation></semantics></math>, and equals <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> elsewhere.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baselines</span>: We compare our method with: (1) Q-learning UCB (QUCB) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jin et al., 2018</a>)</cite>; (2) Q-learning UCB, but additionally incorporates a momentum term that is built from the value functions for each state-action pair (UCBMQ) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Menard et al., 2021</a>)</cite>; (3) a model-based RL baseline which directly adds a UCB bonus to the Q-values (UCBVI) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Azar et al. (2017)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.1.2 </span>Frozen-Lake</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fig. <a href="#A2.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Appendix B Experimental details" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> (c) shows our <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[4]\times[4]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>4</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[4]\times[4]</annotation></semantics></math> FrozenLake environment with <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math> states and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> actions (left, right, up, down). This is a more challenging setting than GridWorld, as it involves crossing a frozen lake from the start to the goal without falling into any holes by walking across the frozen lake. When the agent uses its policy to take action, it will move in the corresponding direction following the action with probability <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, and move in either perpendicular direction with equal probability (i.e., <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon/2</annotation></semantics></math>) in both directions. The starting position is <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. The reward is equal to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> in state <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(4,4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(4,4)</annotation></semantics></math> and is zero elsewhere. The episode ends if the agent moves to the hole or reaches the goal. We set the planning horizon <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=500" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>500</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=500</annotation></semantics></math> and the number of episodes <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=60000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=60000</annotation></semantics></math>. From the first episode to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{K}=20000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>20000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{K}=20000</annotation></semantics></math>, the noise is <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, from episode <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20000</annotation></semantics></math>-th to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{K}=40000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>40000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{K}=40000</annotation></semantics></math>, the noise <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=1/2</annotation></semantics></math>. After that, the transition function is shifted by changing <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=2/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=2/3</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">State</span>: The state <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}=(i,j)\in[8]\times[8]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>8</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}=(i,j)\in[8]\times[8]</annotation></semantics></math> at step <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> consists of the agent’s position on the grid, where <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is the row and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> is the column index. <span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Action</span>: Action <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}\in\{left,right,up,down\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}\in\{left,right,up,down\}</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is the direction in which the agent will try to reach. <span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">State Transition Function</span>: From position state <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the next position of the agent <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> will follow action <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> with probability <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, and move in either perpendicular direction with equal probability (i.e., <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon/2</annotation></semantics></math>) in both directions. <span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reward Function</span>: The reward <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> equals <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> when the agent reaches the final state <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(8,8)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(8,8)</annotation></semantics></math>, and equals <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> elsewhere.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baselines</span>: Similarly to the GridWorld task, we compare our method with the following tabular UCB-based RL baselines: (1) QUCB <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jin et al., 2018</a>)</cite>; (2) UCBMQ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Menard et al., 2021</a>)</cite>; (3) UCBVI <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Azar et al. (2017)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.1.3 </span>CartPole</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fig. <a href="#A2.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Appendix B Experimental details" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> (c) shows this task with 4 continuous state features (cart position, cart velocity, pole angle, pole angular velocity), and 2 actions (left, right). The goal of each episode is to keep the pole upright as long as possible, and the reward is <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+1</annotation></semantics></math> for each step taken. We set the number of episodes <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=800" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>800</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=800</annotation></semantics></math>. After episode <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{K}=400" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>400</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{K}=400</annotation></semantics></math>, the shift occurs by adding Gaussian noise <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(0,0.15)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.15</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(0,0.15)</annotation></semantics></math> to the cart and pole angular velocity features.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">State</span>: The state <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{4}</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> consists the following positions and velocities: (1) the cart position can take values between <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-4.8,4.8)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4.8</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>4.8</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-4.8,4.8)</annotation></semantics></math>, but the episode terminates if the cart leaves the <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-2.4,2.4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2.4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2.4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-2.4,2.4)</annotation></semantics></math> range; (2) the cart velocity can take values between <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-\infty,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-\infty,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>; (3) the pole angle can be observed between <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-0.418,0.148)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.418</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0.148</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-0.418,0.148)</annotation></semantics></math> radians, but the episode terminates if the pole angle is not in the range <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-0.2095,0.2095)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.2095</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0.2095</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-0.2095,0.2095)</annotation></semantics></math>; (4) the pole angular velocity can take values between <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-\infty,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-\infty,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Action</span>: The action <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> indicates the direction of the fixed force with which the cart is driven, where <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> represents pushing the cart to the left and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> represents pushing the cart to the right.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">State Transition Function</span>: From the state <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the cart changed its positions and velocities to state <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> by action <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, with additional Gaussian noise <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\sim\mathcal{N}(0,0.15)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.15</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\sim\mathcal{N}(0,0.15)</annotation></semantics></math> to the cart and pole angular velocity features. All observations are assigned a uniformly random value in <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-0.05,0.05)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0.05</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-0.05,0.05)</annotation></semantics></math>. The episode ends if any one of the following occurs: (1) Termination: the pole angle is over <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm 0.2095" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>0.2095</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm 0.2095</annotation></semantics></math> or the cart position is over <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm 2.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>2.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm 2.4</annotation></semantics></math> (center of the cart reaches the edge of the display); (2) Truncation: episode length is greater than <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="200" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>200</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">200</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reward Function</span>: Since the goal is to keep the pole upright as long as possible, a reward <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is added by <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+1</annotation></semantics></math> for step <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, including the termination step. The reward threshold is <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="195" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>195</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">195</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baselines</span>: We compare our method with: (1) Random policy; (2) Deep Q-Network (DQN) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mnih et al., 2013</a>; <a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Paszke et al., 2019</a>)</cite>; (3) Deep Q-Network with UCB exploration (DQN-UCB). We adapt the hashing technique of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tang et al. (2017)</a></cite> to count the number of visited pairs <math id="A2.SS1.SSS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{h}(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{h}(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math> on this continuous state space. In particular, count-based exploration uses a static hashing to map continuous states into discrete states and then counts the number of times a given state has been visited. After that, the UCB algorithms are trained with a bonus reward considering the number of times we have visited the state. This bonus reward plays the role of exploration.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.1.4 </span>COVID-19 patient hospital allocation</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Notation</span>:</p>
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>: Number of hospitals.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>: Number of days in the planning horizon.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>: Capacity of hospital <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\cdots,K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\cdots,K</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>: Number of arriving COVID-19 patients in the system on day <math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{A_{t}\}_{t\in[T]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{A_{t}\}_{t\in[T]}</annotation></semantics></math>: Stochastic process representing the number of arriving COVID-19 patients over time.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math>: Number of non-COVID patients in hospital <math id="A2.I1.i6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> on day <math id="A2.I1.i6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{D_{i,t}\}_{t\in[T]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{D_{i,t}\}_{t\in[T]}</annotation></semantics></math>: Stochastic process representing the number of non-COVID patients in hospital <math id="A2.I1.i7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> over time.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math> (action): Number of arriving COVID-19 patients allocated to hospital <math id="A2.I1.i8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> on day <math id="A2.I1.i8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i9" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math>: COVID-19 patient occupancy in hospital <math id="A2.I1.i9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> on day <math id="A2.I1.i9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i10" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i10.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math>: Total occupancy in hospital <math id="A2.I1.i10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> on day <math id="A2.I1.i10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, defined as <math id="A2.I1.i10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{i,t}=d_{i,t}+y_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{i,t}=d_{i,t}+y_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i11" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i11.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>: Random variable representing patient length of stay.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i12" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i12.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(L_{i}\geq t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(L_{i}\geq t)</annotation></semantics></math>: Probability that a patient at hospital <math id="A2.I1.i12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> stays at least <math id="A2.I1.i12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> days.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i13" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i13.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>: Parameter for updating the estimated COVID-19 occupancy.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i14" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i14.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>: State of the system at time <math id="A2.I1.i14.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">State</span>: State <math id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{2K+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{2K+1}</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> consists of the COVID-19 and non-COVID-19 occupancies in each hospital, along with the number of arriving patients:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E82.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle s_{t}=(y_{1,t},y_{2,t},\cdots,y_{K,t};\quad d_{1,t},d_{2,t},\cdots,d_{K,t};\quad N_{t})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">;</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">;</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle s_{t}=(y_{1,t},y_{2,t},\cdots,y_{K,t};\quad d_{1,t},d_{2,t},\cdots,d_{K,t};\quad N_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(82)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Action</span>: Action <math id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> at time t consists of the number of COVID-19 patients allocated to each hospital:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx60" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a_{t}=(a_{1,t},a_{2,t},\cdots,a_{K,t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a_{t}=(a_{1,t},a_{2,t},\cdots,a_{K,t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(83)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">subject to the constraints: <math id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{N}a_{i,t}=N_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{N}a_{i,t}=N_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{i,t}\geq 0,\forall i=1\cdots K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i,t}\geq 0,\forall i=1\cdots K</annotation></semantics></math>. To allocate <math id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> patients to satisfy this constraint, we use an oracle function from <math id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>-values, which receives <math id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> patients and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>-values, then outputs action <math id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> hospitals <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zuo and Joe-Wong, 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">State Transition Function</span>:
The number of arriving COVID-19 patients is sampled from the corresponding stochastic process:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx61" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle N_{t+1}\sim A_{t+1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle N_{t+1}\sim A_{t+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(84)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The non-COVID-19 occupancy is sampled from the corresponding stochastic process (can be deterministic):</p>
<table id="A2.EGx62" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d_{i,t+1}\sim D_{i,t+1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d_{i,t+1}\sim D_{i,t+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(85)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The COVID-19 occupancy update:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx63" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y_{i,t+1}=\beta_{i}\cdot y_{i,t}+a_{i,t+1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y_{i,t+1}=\beta_{i}\cdot y_{i,t}+a_{i,t+1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(86)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is provided by the environment, which can be done by minimizing the difference between the estimated and actual COVID-19 occupancies from the real-world dataset: COVID-19 Reported Patient Impact and Hospital Capacity by Facility, provided by the U.S. Department of Health &amp; Human Services over <math id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=1274" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1274</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=1274</annotation></semantics></math> days from 2020 to 2024. We use the <math id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=40</annotation></semantics></math> dataset collected from Texas hospitals.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reward Function</span>: The number of overflows across all hospitals:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx64" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E87.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle r_{t}=\sum_{i=1}^{K}-\max(0,o_{i,t+1}-c_{i})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mi>max</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{t}=\sum_{i=1}^{K}-\max(0,o_{i,t+1}-c_{i}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(87)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p6.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{i,t+1}=y_{i,t+1}+d_{i,t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{i,t+1}=y_{i,t+1}+d_{i,t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the total occupancy of hospital <math id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+1</annotation></semantics></math>. This represents the cost of a capacity shortage.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baselines</span>: We compare our method with: (1-2) combinatorial resource allocation UCB methods, i.e., UCB_RA and CUCB_RA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zuo and Joe-Wong, 2021</a>)</cite>. And our Deep Q-learning extension, including (3) Deep Q-learning only (CNeural_RA, i.e., DQN) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mnih et al., 2013</a>; <a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Paszke et al., 2019</a>)</cite>, and (4) Deep Q-learning with UCB exploration (Q-learning, i.e., DQN-UCB).</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS5" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.1.5 </span>Source code and computing systems</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our source code includes the dataset scripts, setup for the environment, and our provided code (details in README.md). We run our code on a single GPU: NVIDIA RTX A6000-49140MiB with 8-CPUs: AMD Ryzen Threadripper 3960X 24-Core with 8GB RAM per each and require 10GB available disk space for storage.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Demo notebook code for Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3 Shift-Aware Density Q-Learning UCB" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td"></td>
<td id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">
<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:468.3pt;">
<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_language_python ltx_lstlisting ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing"><span class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></span>
<span id="lstnumberx1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_keyword ltx_font_bold">from</span><span id="lstnumberx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">rlberry</span>.<span id="lstnumberx1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">agents</span><span id="lstnumberx1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_keyword ltx_font_bold">import</span><span id="lstnumberx1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">IncrementalAgent</span>,<span id="lstnumberx1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">DiscreteCounter</span>
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx2" class="ltx_listingline">
</span>
<span id="lstnumberx3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_keyword ltx_font_bold">class</span><span id="lstnumberx3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">Ours</span>(<span id="lstnumberx3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">IncrementalAgent</span>):
</span>
